Detecting emerging wildfires in real-time is crucial for safeguarding life and property, as well as protecting natural resources and minimizing ecological damage. This study introduces the development of algorithms that leverage the Google Cloud Vision API to identify wildfires within image datasets. All algorithms were tested using the publicly available "UCI Machine Learning – Image Classification – Wildfire" dataset. The API was configured with English training data concerning "wildfire" classification. The study examines the efficacy of several strategies to detect wildfires visually, including:
1. Classifying entire images in their current state;
2. Applying predefined training images representing what to look out for;
3. Utilizing crop image regions to focus detection.
Finally, the research compares two distinct methods of sending images to the API to determine their effectiveness.

